WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.533
The primary colours.

2
00:00:01.693 --> 00:00:04.200
Red, yellow and blue are the primary colours.

3
00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:06.636
You cannot make them by mixing other colours.

4
00:00:06.796 --> 00:00:09.629
But you can make almost every other colour by mixing them.

5
00:00:09.789 --> 00:00:12.204
That is why every paint box has them.

6
00:00:12.904 --> 00:00:13.786
Mixing.

7
00:00:13.946 --> 00:00:15.478
Red and yellow make orange.

8
00:00:15.638 --> 00:00:17.171
Red and blue make purple.

9
00:00:17.331 --> 00:00:18.817
Blue and yellow make green.

10
00:00:18.977 --> 00:00:20.510
Before you mix, guess.

11
00:00:20.670 --> 00:00:22.063
Then mix, and look.

12
00:00:22.223 --> 00:00:24.359
What actually happened is what you learn.

13
00:00:25.059 --> 00:00:26.220
Light and dark.

14
00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:28.563
Add white to a colour and it gets lighter.

15
00:00:28.723 --> 00:00:30.441
Add black and it gets darker.

16
00:00:30.601 --> 00:00:33.852
How light or dark a colour is has a name: tone.

17
00:00:34.012 --> 00:00:37.355
You can put colours in a ladder from the lightest to the darkest.

18
00:00:38.055 --> 00:00:39.263
Warm and cool.

19
00:00:39.423 --> 00:00:42.813
Red, orange and yellow feel warm, like fire and sunshine.

20
00:00:42.973 --> 00:00:45.202
Blue feels cool, like water and ice.

21
00:00:45.362 --> 00:00:48.984
Artists choose warm or cool colours to make you feel something.

22
00:00:49.684 --> 00:00:51.124
Colour in a cloth.

23
00:00:51.284 --> 00:00:54.999
A weaver makes cloth in coloured stripes that come back again and again.

24
00:00:55.159 --> 00:00:57.063
Every colour was chosen on purpose.

25
00:00:57.223 --> 00:00:58.616
Cloth is art too.
